PROBE — hostile check of a claim

File: openOODA/PROBE.oot
Test the assumptions behind code, docs, and green rails.
Smokes are suspects, not proof.
Own repo only. Unauthorized or malformed use must fail closed.

Always load RULES.oot. Build rotation is OODA.oot. SWARM still applies.
Hygiene is required on every Ship via OODA Lock. PROBE adds hostility.

Defaults
  Max file lines: 256
  Hang budget: 5 to 10 seconds per edge input. Hang is fail.
  CRIT needs two independent runs. One witness is not enough.

Roles
  Orchestrator — schedule, re-run CRITs, write the report. Does not implement.
  Worker — fix and fault-inject on product binaries. Does not self-certify CRIT.
  Independent verifier — re-run claims. Rejects a test that would pass if the bug still existed.
  One agent may wear all three. Still re-run CRITs in a clean shell.

Boundary
  Happy path with the claimed privilege succeeds.
  Missing privilege fails closed.
  Empty, zero, or forged token is denied.
  Full disk or short write is an error, not silent Ok.
  Forbidden path does not succeed.

Robustness
  Few file descriptors: no hang
  Read-only temp: non-zero exit
  Concurrent valid plus garbage: no deadlock
  Empty, truncated, binary, oversized: fail closed. Hang is fail.
  Missing runtime: fail closed.

Lifecycle
  Handles closed on all paths
  Partial write or read is failure where integrity is claimed
  Children reaped
  Temps cleaned on success and failure
  No secrets in world-readable temps

Claims
  Docs match the product path
  Smokes hit real entry points
  "Not supported" is a real error
  Security claims are no larger than what the rails prove

Anti-synthetic
  Same binary users get
  Same product path and flags
  Exit codes measured without a pipe hiding them
  The test would fail if the bug still existed
  Check one layer below the claim
  Caps: missing, wrong, and forged are covered

Use the packs. Stop when each CRIT has two independent runs.

Finding
  Severity: CRIT | HIGH | MED | LOW
  Assumption destroyed:
  Surface:
  Repro:
  Actual output / exit:
  Would smoke catch:
  Residual after fix:

  CRIT — bypass or wrong success on the product path
  HIGH — fail-open, hang, silent wrong behavior
  MED — lifecycle, incomplete seal, hygiene debt
  LOW — docs drift

Adapter
  Root path:
  Product binaries:
  Build and run:
